      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "@here what do you think about having a large PTH as the pin1 marker. \nThat allows someone to solder in a header pin into their motherboard that would force orientation. \n@RebelMike One thing about the circle in the wirebonding footprint is that it will likely be covered in black and you won't be able to see it anymore. ?Ideally? this sits far enough outside to stay clear of gunk (I made it much larger than it needs to be to account for process variabilities and things likely being done by hand)",
